  "_provenance": {
    "what": "A Flight Offers Search v2 response, JFK-LHR, one adult, 2026-11-12.",
    "captured": false,
    "how": "SYNTHESISED from Amadeus's published Flight Offers Search v2 schema. Unlike kiwi-jfk-lhr.json, which is a real response recorded off the wire, no Amadeus credential was available on the machine this was written on, so nothing here was observed. The SHAPE is from the documentation; the VALUES are constructed to exercise the adapter.",
    "therefore": "It proves the adapter handles the documented schema. It does NOT prove the documented schema matches what the service returns. Replace it with a real capture on the first successful `live.py probe` and re-run the adapter tests; a field that moved will show up as a dropped itinerary, not as silence.",
    "exercises": [
      "a nonstop with a BASIC brand carrying no checked bag",
      "the same physical flight on an upsold brand that includes one - the bags-flip pair",
      "a codeshare where operating.carrierCode differs from carrierCode",
      "an offer where operating is ABSENT, which in this schema means the marketing carrier flies it",
      "a two-segment connection on one ticket, so bags are through-checked",
      "an itinerary through an uncurated airport, which must be dropped rather than guessed"
    ]
  },
